<Ui xmlns="http://www.blizzard.com/wow/ui/" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.blizzard.com/wow/ui/ ..\..\FrameXML\UI.xsd">
	<!--
		LFG Forever's settings row for a line of text: the "Message" fields under
		"Auto-whisper on Ask to Join" and "Auto-whisper on Invite". Blizzard ships
		no text-input settings row, so this is one of our own, laid out like
		Blizzard's rows:

		* the Text label, as SettingsListElementTemplate's
		  (Blizzard_SettingControls.xml:49-53); the mixin anchors it on Init;
		* a Tooltip hover area over the label holding Blizzard's HoverBackground
		  highlight, as that template's (:56-69); the mixin gives it its
		  tooltip on Init;
		* the "?" at the right, which lists the row's placeholders;
		* the EditBox where Blizzard's controls sit: from the row's centre
		  minus 80 (Blizzard_SettingControls.lua:592) to just before the "?".

		IT INHERITS NO BLIZZARD ROW AND TAKES NO BLIZZARD ROW MIXIN, and no frame
		of it declares a script. Blizzard's settings list builds the row inside
		a protected call, then reads it outside one (ScrollBoxListView.lua:111,
		:361-395). Built on Blizzard's row template and mixins, the row carried
		Blizzard's methods as values of ours, the list read one of them tainted,
		and every row built after it, the Keybindings page's included, ran as
		LFG Forever. The only mixin is ours, holding only the methods Blizzard
		calls inside its protected calls. .claude/rules/settings-list-taint.md
	-->
	<Frame name="WildSparkWildGroupsSettingsMessageRowTemplate" mixin="WildSparkWildGroupsSettingsMessageRowMixin" virtual="true">
		<Size x="280" y="26"/>
		<Layers>
			<Layer level="OVERLAY">
				<FontString parentKey="Text" inherits="GameFontNormal" justifyH="LEFT" wordwrap="false"/>
			</Layer>
		</Layers>
		<Frames>
			<Frame parentKey="Tooltip">
				<Anchors>
					<Anchor point="TOPLEFT"/>
					<Anchor point="BOTTOMRIGHT" relativePoint="BOTTOM" x="-80"/>
				</Anchors>
				<Layers>
					<Layer level="BACKGROUND">
						<Texture parentKey="HoverBackground" inherits="HoverBackgroundTemplate"/>
					</Layer>
				</Layers>
			</Frame>
			<Frame parentKey="Help">
				<Size x="20" y="20"/>
				<Anchors>
					<Anchor point="TOPRIGHT" x="-20" y="-3"/>
				</Anchors>
				<Layers>
					<Layer level="OVERLAY">
						<FontString parentKey="Text" inherits="GameFontNormal" text="?">
							<Anchors>
								<Anchor point="CENTER"/>
							</Anchors>
						</FontString>
					</Layer>
				</Layers>
			</Frame>
			<EditBox parentKey="EditBox" inherits="InputBoxTemplate" autoFocus="false">
				<Size y="20"/>
				<Anchors>
					<Anchor point="TOPLEFT" relativePoint="TOP" x="-75" y="-3"/>
					<Anchor point="TOPRIGHT" relativeKey="$parent.Help" relativePoint="TOPLEFT" x="-4" y="0"/>
				</Anchors>
			</EditBox>
		</Frames>
	</Frame>

	<!--
		LFG Forever's settings row for a sentence: the one in Miscellaneous that
		says where the other languages come from. Blizzard's only text row,
		SettingsAddOnDisabledLabelTemplate (Blizzard_SettingControls.xml:36-47),
		shows one fixed string and has no code to change it, so this is one of
		our own, laid out like it: the text at x = 37, where every label starts.
		It wraps across the row to 20 short of its right edge (the "?" margin
		above), centred on the row.

		THE HEIGHT IS FIXED. The list takes a row's height from its template
		(Blizzard_SettingsList.lua:68-71), and nothing of ours may change that.
		45 is the height of Blizzard's section header (:13) and holds three lines
		of GameFontNormal; maxLines cuts a longer translation short instead of
		drawing it over the row below.

		The same rule as the row above: no Blizzard row, no Blizzard row mixin,
		no script. The mixin holds Init alone. .claude/rules/language-packs-row.md
	-->
	<Frame name="WildSparkWildGroupsSettingsTextRowTemplate" mixin="WildSparkWildGroupsSettingsTextRowMixin" virtual="true">
		<Size x="280" y="45"/>
		<Layers>
			<Layer level="OVERLAY">
				<FontString parentKey="Text" inherits="GameFontNormal" justifyH="LEFT" justifyV="MIDDLE" maxLines="3">
					<Anchors>
						<Anchor point="LEFT" x="37"/>
						<Anchor point="RIGHT" x="-20"/>
					</Anchors>
				</FontString>
			</Layer>
		</Layers>
	</Frame>
</Ui>
